WEBVTT

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.340
I... I...

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.340
I love you, Onii-chan!

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:43.980
Snow White Recollections

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.740
Is today April Fool's?

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.130
No...

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.790
It's not Labor Day either.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.540
I've watch you grow since
you were this small.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.900
I think of you as my precious
younger sister...

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.970
but it's nothing more than that...

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:35.680
Elis!

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.960
What am I going to do?

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.540
Elis, how long are you going
to sleep? Wake up!

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:18.240
Eat your salad. Your eggs, too.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.180
Okay.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.550
It's supposed to rain this evening.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:26.680
Okay.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.240
Take an umbrella.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.490
Okay. I'm done eating.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:31.720
Eat all your...

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.590
Looks like you did.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.570
I guess I'll just have to act
like I always do with Elis.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.710
Make sure you don't forget
your umbrella!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.710
Hey, Elis!

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:54.130
I know.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.590
Huh?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.460
What ominous clouds.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.540
Is there something in my hair?

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.040
I'm impressed, Shota-kun.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.640
Huh? About what?

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.220
I can't be kind like you.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.680
I know.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.300
I must have a shallow heart.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.530
Kindness doesn't come naturally to me.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:49.200
Scallops, botamochi, Botan...

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:49.770
Here it is!

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:53.400
Botan... a deciduous tree from China.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.480
Known as the king of flowers...

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.160
Its broad leaves turn white, purple,
and yellow in May...

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.430
What are you doing?

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.210
I was just looking something up.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:09.720
I thought I might use a flower
motif in my novel...

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.970
and was doing some research.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.030
Hokkaido... Hmm...

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.580
Why are you so quiet? It's a little scary.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.440
Really?

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.580
You're going to study abroad
in France, aren't you?

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:32.050
I don't know. I haven't decided yet.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.650
What? I'd leave everything
behind for a chance to go.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.460
Is France really that great a place?

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.540
Come on!

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.620
Elis, it's Paris!

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:45.090
The Eiffel Tower! Bonjour!

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.020
So?

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.070
I guess we don't agree with each other!

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.970
That could be one of your
positive qualities, though.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.160
Oh, Nusamae Bridge.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.150
Studying abroad in France, huh?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.260
Is she going with Kamikura-sensei?

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:31.580
I wish I could go to France.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:34.650
Don't mind them.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:37.140
Thanks, but I'm fine now.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.040
I see.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:47.050
Improve yourself before
you criticize others.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:07:00.480
I can't believe I forgot my umbrella.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.070
Faculty Office

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.030
Hiroki?

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.580
What's wrong?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.020
You look like the world's about to end.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:13.610
Huh?

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.930
Is that what I look like?

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.160
Did something happen?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.000
I love you, Onii-chan!

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:24.820
No, I'm just hungry.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.200
Do you want to go fishing Sunday?

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.170
Fishing? Kiri, you fish?

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:37.180
A friend took me fishing in college.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.990
Turns out it's pretty fun,
so I go once in a while.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:43.110
The forecast said it should
stop raining tonight.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:48.310
Maybe I'll pack a delicious lunch.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.420
Let's go, then.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.860
Where's my fishing pole?

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:08.600
I'll catch a big one so you can have
some delicious sashimi, Elis.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:09.990
There it is.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:17.910
Elis!

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.840
Tomorrow, I'm...

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:22.790
Huh?

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.620
Elis, are you in the bathroom?

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:28.320
Hey!

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:30.540
Elis!

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:44.740
She's late!

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:48.170
I don't know where she's off
to, but she's really late!

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:01.380
Looks like Elis didn't take
her phone with her.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.560
I've gone to see my grandmother.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.390
Don't worry about me.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:10.310
Elis.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:25.340
She should have told me she'd be
going to see her grandmother!

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.110
She could have said something!

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.390
It's tomorrow...

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.320
The anniversary of her parents' death.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:55.760
I've been remembering the past lately.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.640
Do you remember, Elis?

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.650
The day your father and mother
took you to ride a pony.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:08.370
You can do it, Elis!

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.260
Elis!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.860
What's wrong? You're
not scared, are you?

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:22.220
Elis, the pony looks so sad.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:38.660
You spent the whole day
at the ranch crying...

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:42.120
but when you got home you wouldn't
stop talking about horses.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.190
I don't remember that at all.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.580
I suppose you wouldn't.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.000
I think you were still two
years old at the time.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.060
Of course you don't remember.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:52.630
Sorry.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:57.350
I forgot all about the civil servant
exam paperwork I have to do.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:59.940
I'm feeling a little under
the weather, too.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.500
I understand.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:03.820
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:06.000
We'll go fishing together next time.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:07.580
Okay.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:13.320
What am I going to do with all this food?

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:19.030
I shouldn't be going fishing
with Kiri now, anyway.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.220
Elis might call any minute.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.690
I should call her.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:25.990
No, I shouldn't.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.120
Don't worry about her.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.960
She left a note and her phone.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.700
She probably doesn't want to talk to me.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.290
I should just wait for her to come home.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:57.960
I hardly remember anything
about my parents.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:02.110
You once celebrated your
mother's birthday...

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.640
with a crown of flowers just like those.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.010
I did it!

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:14.510
Good job! Shouldn't this crown
be bigger, though?

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:15.380
Bigger?

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.840
Don't you think mom would look
good wearing a big crown?

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:21.390
Yeah, a big and beautiful one!

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.130
I wonder if we'll have enough meat.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:29.330
I know. Elis' appetite has
been growing lately.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.600
Oh?

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.550
Happy birthday, mom!

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:39.230
Looks good on you, mom.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.040
It really does.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.140
Thank you, Elis.

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:43.550
You look cute, mom!

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.010
Mom...

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:11.560
Eating lunch by myself isn't bad either.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.760
I'm choking!

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.410
Here you are.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.190
Superintendent...

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.490
What a delicious looking lunch.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.050
Are you having a picnic?

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:29.020
Yes. I was stood up, so
I'm here by myself.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:34.790
Would you and your dog like to join me?

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:41.810
Some time ago, your mother saw the
pictures you drew on the wall...

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.860
and said you were a genius.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:46.680
Your father said she was just
blind with parental love.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:50.920
It seems Anna-san's assessment
was correct, though.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:53.010
I don't know about that.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.410
You took first place in the
contest, didn't you?

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.250
Huh?

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.950
Hiroki told me about it over the phone.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.180
He said he knew you could do it.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:03.390
He sounded so happy,
I thought he had won.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.390
Onii-chan...

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:09.330
He's my grandchild as well, but
he never comes to see me.

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.300
What's wrong?

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.810
Why don't we go home and have lunch?

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:22.840
Grandma, would it be all right if
I stayed with you a little longer?

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.480
Kiri?

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.170
I'm sorry we couldn't meet today!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:33.140
I ended up meeting someone and
having a fun lunch after all.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:35.920
That corn you like so
much was a big hit.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.510
Corn?

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.790
I'm sorry your friend could not show up.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:47.460
I was rather fortunate to be
treated to lunch, however.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.540
I should be thanking you.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.240
I didn't know what I was going
to do with all this food.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:56.750
I should get going. Thank
you for the food.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.480
See you tomorrow.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:03.210
I'm really disappointed I didn't
get to eat your lunch!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.620
I promise we'll make up for this soon!

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.520
Is lunch the only thing on your mind?

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:31.070
I can't do this. I've got to call her.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:34.760
Hiroki?

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:39.090
Grandma? I was just thinking
of calling you.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:44.620
You should stop by once in a while. I'm
starting to forget what you look like.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:45.700
Sorry.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.160
Elis is with you, isn't she?

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:50.180
Yes, she's here.

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:52.030
Is Elis all right?

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:53.680
She seems fine.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.480
She was staying with you until
yesterday, wasn't she?

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:58.170
Well, yes...

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:01.240
Did something happen there?

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.540
Not really.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:06.900
She's just, you know, a difficult age.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.070
Taking care of her is a lot of work.

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.650
Your favorite corn is in season now.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:18.960
Corn, huh? I just missed
my chance to eat some.

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:30.500
Quiet, everyone.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:35.040
Nice composition. Also...

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:36.770
Mom.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.580
Watch quietly from over there, Elis.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.000
Okay.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:48.990
Hiroki-kun, the energy
in this work is great.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.820
It must have been since then...

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:27.690
Hiroki

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:27.690
I loved Onii-chan since then...

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:33.100
I've watch you grow since
you were this small.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.540
I wonder what's wrong with Elis-chan.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.910
I heard from Kamikura-sensei
she has a cold.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.530
She seemed fine on Saturday.

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:52.550
When I talked to Hosen a couple days
ago, I thought something seemed off.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:17:59.890
Oh, my!

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:04.830
I've come to eat corn!

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:08.170
Come in. I'm delighted you're here.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.770
Come on in.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.640
Grandma, where's Elis?

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.810
That's odd. She was out on
the terrace a moment ago.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.630
How is Elis' cold?

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:47.740
She's feeling a lot better. It's
nothing to worry about.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:56.950
I knew it.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.320
Elis...

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:05.540
Did you finish all your paperwork?

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.920
Let me know if there's anything
I can do to help!

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.390
I've got it covered.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.630
Onii-chan, when did you get here?

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.160
Just now.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.930
You're late for school.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.710
There's no way I can make
it on time now.

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:33.680
I've taken care of it.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:42.030
Make sure you pay your respects.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.230
This place is too far to visit often.

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:46.260
I know.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:57.140
Where are you now, Hiroki?

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.600
Where are you?

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:21.030
I wish you could stay a little longer.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.810
Sorry. We'll be back again.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.970
Grandma, thank you for everything.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:30.410
Come back soon.

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:33.040
Okay.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:47.010
Grandma told me all sorts of
stories about my parents.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.060
I see.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:53.000
I remembered all the fun I used to have.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:57.520
Really? I bet you're glad you came, then.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.330
Yeah.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.170
I'm glad I did.

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:13.450
It's a strange color.

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:16.140
It's pale yellow of a wavering heart.

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:17.440
Hey, Onii-chan...

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:21.110
What's the best way to
make up with a man?

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:23.760
Being honest is the best approach.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:24.730
I'm sorry.

00:23:24.730 --> 00:23:25.620
Exactly.

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:26.910
It was my fault.

00:23:26.910 --> 00:23:27.950
Exactly, exactly.

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:30.570
If I could say that, I wouldn't
have so much trouble!

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:31.650
That's no good!

00:23:31.650 --> 00:23:33.980
Next episode, “Light Yellow Distance.”

00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:35.710
A loss in love is actually a victory!

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:36.920
What?

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:38.320
Really?
